1
00:01:50,840 --> 00:01:53,509
The cargo's coming into
the city from the east.

2
00:01:53,592 --> 00:01:56,262
We're taking the whole vehicle.

3
00:01:57,096 --> 00:01:58,931
Haul's two 'n' a half mil.

4
00:01:59,014 --> 00:02:01,725
Pot o' gold with the usual split.

5
00:02:03,352 --> 00:02:07,523
This one's definitely
the biggest job I've ever taken.

6
00:02:08,232 --> 00:02:10,109
Target's a corp, ain't it?

7
00:02:10,192 --> 00:02:12,903
Three guesses which one it is.

8
00:02:13,696 --> 00:02:16,157
Arasaka, of course.

9
00:02:16,740 --> 00:02:19,994
Half a mil a head's nice 'n' all,
but I ain't even sure if it's worth it.

10
00:02:20,077 --> 00:02:23,080
Really think five of us is enough?

11
00:02:23,164 --> 00:02:26,167
Security footprint
on the convoy's peculiarly small.

12
00:02:26,750 --> 00:02:31,505
Arasaka's posted a limited crew to cast
a short shadow, keep a low profile.

13
00:02:31,589 --> 00:02:33,966
We'll strike the metal where it's soft.

14
00:02:34,049 --> 00:02:36,051
I dunno, man…

15
00:02:36,135 --> 00:02:38,179
Let's not overthink this.

16
00:02:38,262 --> 00:02:41,307
Smash, grab, deliver. It's what we do.

17
00:02:41,390 --> 00:02:43,058
Business as usual.

18
00:02:43,142 --> 00:02:45,769
Business as usual my ass.

19
00:02:46,437 --> 00:02:49,565
You think he'll withstand
the cyberskeleton?

20
00:02:51,400 --> 00:02:56,780
Arasaka does. After seeing his chemistry
mesh so well with the Sandevistan.

21
00:02:56,864 --> 00:03:03,329
Tanaka wanted him back in the Academy
so he could test the cyberskeleton on him.

22
00:03:03,412 --> 00:03:07,082
And this girl was trying to
bury that information

23
00:03:07,166 --> 00:03:09,960
so no one would come after him.

24
00:03:10,044 --> 00:03:13,881
That's how I see it.
Frying Tanaka tied up a loose end.

25
00:03:14,882 --> 00:03:19,011
Maine and Dorio were just
collateral damage in her schemes.

26
00:03:19,553 --> 00:03:21,305
That's one way of putting it…

27
00:03:21,388 --> 00:03:24,808
So much carnage for one so petite.

28
00:03:24,892 --> 00:03:28,103
How many did she kill just to save one?

29
00:03:35,694 --> 00:03:40,824
Dove a little deeper and found that
she used to work for Arasaka.

30
00:03:40,908 --> 00:03:43,911
They groomed her
to mine data in the Old Net.

31
00:03:44,828 --> 00:03:48,082
Guess that's how she's been able to
get past Arasaka's ICE.

32
00:03:49,708 --> 00:03:51,001
This is perfect.

33
00:03:51,085 --> 00:03:56,966
What a wonderful surprise.
We can dangle her in front of Arasaka.

34
00:03:57,049 --> 00:04:00,261
Our fast-lane ticket up
the corporate rungs!

35
00:04:00,344 --> 00:04:03,222
Didn't see you as
such a simp corpo-climber.

36
00:04:03,305 --> 00:04:05,224
Is that really so strange?

37
00:04:05,307 --> 00:04:07,601
What are fixers
if not glorified pet owners

38
00:04:07,685 --> 00:04:10,062
who keep their mercenary hounds well fed?

39
00:04:10,646 --> 00:04:15,943
The only way to succeed in Night City
is to get in with the corporations.

40
00:04:16,026 --> 00:04:19,238
I'll require your continued assistance.

41
00:04:19,321 --> 00:04:22,157
Gonna make me keep digging
this hole deeper?

42
00:04:22,241 --> 00:04:25,286
This is a great opportunity
for you as well.

43
00:04:25,369 --> 00:04:29,832
I have corporate amnesty for
the Tanaka incident… But what about you?

44
00:04:29,915 --> 00:04:32,668
You're as slimy as ever.

45
00:04:32,751 --> 00:04:36,005
Let's play nice for old time's sake.

46
00:04:36,088 --> 00:04:42,428
How often do we get to work with Arasaka
and stick it to Militech with one hand?

47
00:04:42,511 --> 00:04:45,306
Arasaka wouldn't object.

48
00:04:45,973 --> 00:04:49,476
I'll negotiate for your immunity
and commission.

49
00:04:51,103 --> 00:04:55,065
Never trust a soul in Night City.

50
00:04:55,858 --> 00:04:58,152
Trusting fools deserve
the hand they're dealt…

51
00:05:00,529 --> 00:05:02,990
Is David a bargaining chip as well?

52
00:05:03,073 --> 00:05:07,369
Naturally. I've conjured a plan.

53
00:05:07,453 --> 00:05:10,456
I'll pitch them both to Arasaka.

54
00:05:23,427 --> 00:05:26,096
What's up with the emergency meeting?

55
00:05:27,056 --> 00:05:31,602
Faraday's come through.
It's our biggest gig yet.

56
00:05:32,186 --> 00:05:37,107
Huge risk, huge return. Turn back now
if you're not ready to face the heat.

57
00:05:42,613 --> 00:05:44,198
I'm counting on you too, Kiwi.

58
00:05:44,281 --> 00:05:45,115
Sure.

59
00:05:45,199 --> 00:05:49,036
Yo, granny and gramps
can bench this round.

60
00:05:49,119 --> 00:05:51,789
Think your little chicken legs'll
reach the pedals?

61
00:05:51,872 --> 00:05:53,332
Kiss my ass.

62
00:05:54,208 --> 00:05:55,501
Give us the brief.

63
00:05:56,293 --> 00:05:58,504
'Saka put on a small,
heavy-duty security squad.

64
00:05:58,587 --> 00:06:03,300
But they'll split. Half'll go after
a diversion squad commissioned by Faraday.

65
00:06:05,094 --> 00:06:06,637
Diversion squad?

66
00:06:06,720 --> 00:06:11,391
A decoy, basically. Though that's probably
not in the brief Faraday gave them.

67
00:06:11,475 --> 00:06:12,518
Oh.

68
00:06:12,601 --> 00:06:14,978
Typical Faraday handiwork.

69
00:06:15,062 --> 00:06:18,023
Of course, there's no way to tell
if we're also a decoy…

70
00:06:19,858 --> 00:06:21,110
Bitch!

71
00:06:56,854 --> 00:07:00,232
Good, good. We've got 'em
nice and split. What's the call?

72
00:07:00,315 --> 00:07:03,944
Main target's off the road.
We've got the high ground.

73
00:07:04,027 --> 00:07:05,863
Put her in gear, Falco!

74
00:07:06,572 --> 00:07:07,447
Alright!

75
00:07:07,531 --> 00:07:08,699
Let's hit it!

76
00:07:10,993 --> 00:07:15,497
Hey, David. Car's all warmed and ready…

77
00:07:15,581 --> 00:07:16,790
David!

78
00:07:17,583 --> 00:07:20,169
Are these all immunosuppressants?

79
00:07:20,252 --> 00:07:25,382
Can you fetch my mom's jacket for me?

80
00:07:25,466 --> 00:07:27,509
We're calling off the gig!

81
00:07:27,593 --> 00:07:31,305
Rebecca… I got a favor to ask…

82
00:07:31,388 --> 00:07:32,890
You better knock it--

83
00:07:32,973 --> 00:07:37,394
Becca, I can't ask anyone else…

84
00:07:48,113 --> 00:07:49,031
Rebecca?

85
00:07:49,114 --> 00:07:52,910
Puppy-dog eyes! Knew I'm
a sucker for the vulnerable, didn't ya?!

86
00:07:52,993 --> 00:07:56,371
Don't use your fucking Sandevistan.
You hear me?

87
00:07:56,455 --> 00:07:57,664
Okay, okay…

88
00:08:12,930 --> 00:08:14,640
One down!

89
00:08:14,723 --> 00:08:17,267
Alright, we're right on the target's ass!

90
00:08:17,351 --> 00:08:18,685
I'll hack into the brake.

91
00:08:18,769 --> 00:08:20,395
Hold on, we got a tail!

92
00:08:24,483 --> 00:08:26,777
Can't even get a peek out there!

93
00:08:26,860 --> 00:08:27,986
Leave it to me!

94
00:08:28,070 --> 00:08:31,740
Hey! Don't use your Sandevistan…

95
00:08:40,415 --> 00:08:42,125
Fucking deaf, that one?!

96
00:08:49,091 --> 00:08:53,637
You're a real piece of work!

97
00:08:53,720 --> 00:08:57,766
Damn you, David!

98
00:09:03,355 --> 00:09:04,815
Everyone good?

99
00:09:04,898 --> 00:09:07,234
Hey 'stache! Do we look good?!

100
00:09:07,317 --> 00:09:08,527
Look.

101
00:09:09,486 --> 00:09:11,113
It's still going?!

102
00:09:11,196 --> 00:09:13,365
ICE is as thick as the armor.
Can't hack it.

103
00:09:13,949 --> 00:09:15,576
Then I'll hit 'em from the front.

104
00:09:15,659 --> 00:09:16,785
Seriously, knock it--

105
00:09:17,911 --> 00:09:20,914
Fucking tired of being ignored!

106
00:09:26,044 --> 00:09:28,463
…on autopilot!

107
00:10:10,756 --> 00:10:14,259
So please.
Sit back, relax, and enjoy the show.

108
00:10:16,803 --> 00:10:17,638
Not good.

109
00:10:18,221 --> 00:10:20,891
-We'd better stop it fast before it falls.
-What?!

110
00:10:30,067 --> 00:10:34,279
Alright… What are ya gonna do, David?

111
00:10:34,905 --> 00:10:37,532
We're right on the edge…

112
00:10:37,616 --> 00:10:39,493
Falco! Pull up closer!

113
00:10:39,576 --> 00:10:41,203
Easier said than done…

114
00:10:48,085 --> 00:10:50,379
What do we do?!

115
00:10:50,462 --> 00:10:52,172
I'll shoot it if you won't!

116
00:10:59,721 --> 00:11:03,767
That's right. Easy does it, David.

117
00:11:03,850 --> 00:11:06,895
No one here to slap sense into you now.

118
00:11:07,646 --> 00:11:09,856
Make a choice.

119
00:11:09,940 --> 00:11:13,610
You're special, remember?

120
00:11:24,538 --> 00:11:25,539
Brake!

121
00:11:25,622 --> 00:11:26,873
Slam on 'em!

122
00:12:03,785 --> 00:12:04,953
No way.

123
00:12:05,036 --> 00:12:06,788
Th-That's how it's done.

124
00:12:06,872 --> 00:12:08,373
Bit my tongue…

125
00:12:17,924 --> 00:12:19,384
How nice.

126
00:12:19,968 --> 00:12:24,764
They send an executive-class AV
to collect a street girl?

127
00:12:25,348 --> 00:12:28,018
You really must be
their precious, lost toy.

128
00:12:32,105 --> 00:12:35,233
Still no response from Lucy?

129
00:12:35,317 --> 00:12:39,154
Ugh. What's one more runner
gonna do for us at this point?

130
00:12:39,237 --> 00:12:41,907
You gonna pay her from your pot?

131
00:12:41,990 --> 00:12:43,408
How's it going over there?

132
00:12:43,492 --> 00:12:46,369
Few more minutes to break the lock.

133
00:12:46,453 --> 00:12:50,540
Is it just me or does it bother you
that this carrier was unmanned?

134
00:12:50,624 --> 00:12:53,126
You sure it's an Arasaka vehicle?

135
00:12:53,210 --> 00:12:56,922
If you're so worried,
just take the cargo and go.

136
00:12:57,005 --> 00:12:59,674
We're all waiting on you.

137
00:12:59,758 --> 00:13:03,929
Quit the yapping and let's go get our car.

138
00:13:04,012 --> 00:13:08,975
Sheesh. Didn't strike me back when
we were going after the carrier,

139
00:13:09,059 --> 00:13:13,355
but we'd be fishes in a barrel
if anyone tried to shoot us out here.

140
00:13:13,438 --> 00:13:19,444
Jesus, old man. Nervous fart like you
doesn't deserve that cowboy 'stache!

141
00:13:19,528 --> 00:13:21,696
You'd go weak in the knees if I shaved.

142
00:13:21,780 --> 00:13:24,032
Ew! Gonna kick it off!

143
00:13:24,115 --> 00:13:28,453
Stop dodging, old man!

144
00:13:29,162 --> 00:13:31,915
Looks like the decoy failed.
We've got company!

145
00:13:33,875 --> 00:13:34,960
What?!

146
00:13:43,009 --> 00:13:44,177
That a Basilisk?

147
00:13:44,886 --> 00:13:46,429
And a missile carrier!

148
00:13:46,513 --> 00:13:47,931
You're shitting me…

149
00:13:48,014 --> 00:13:48,932
Militech!

150
00:14:05,240 --> 00:14:09,077
What the fuck?!
Why're we being steamrolled by Militech?!

151
00:14:10,412 --> 00:14:13,582
Faraday's a Militech-man, ain't he?

152
00:14:14,165 --> 00:14:16,418
The fishiness is really starting to reek!

153
00:14:19,879 --> 00:14:20,755
It's open!

154
00:14:20,839 --> 00:14:22,007
That was quick!

155
00:14:22,090 --> 00:14:24,342
Take cover inside. Hurry!

156
00:14:25,135 --> 00:14:27,012
What in the seven hells is this…?

157
00:14:27,095 --> 00:14:30,849
This is what Faraday paid Maine to find?

158
00:14:30,932 --> 00:14:33,143
So what is it?

159
00:14:33,226 --> 00:14:36,855
A cyberskeleton. Military implant.

160
00:14:36,938 --> 00:14:41,026
Military…
You mean like David's Sandevistan?

161
00:14:41,109 --> 00:14:44,487
From what I hear,
it's a whole different caliber.

162
00:14:44,571 --> 00:14:48,617
Hey. This kid's Sandy ain't
nothing to turn your nose up at either.

163
00:14:48,700 --> 00:14:51,328
First time I'm hearing about this.

164
00:14:51,411 --> 00:14:53,204
Believe me or don't.

165
00:14:53,288 --> 00:15:00,128
Arasaka thinks they can overtake Militech
if this thing hits the market.

166
00:15:00,211 --> 00:15:03,048
But they've kept its development
on the down-low.

167
00:15:03,131 --> 00:15:08,637
Most of its information
was concentrated under Tanaka's wing.

168
00:15:08,720 --> 00:15:12,933
I don't know how,
but Faraday got wind of this,

169
00:15:13,016 --> 00:15:17,395
and promised to leak this tech to
Militech to get himself a nice deal.

170
00:15:18,146 --> 00:15:22,150
Not every day you get to fly
above Night City at your leisure.

171
00:15:22,233 --> 00:15:28,406
It must be a nice change of scenery
from your usual ice-filled baths.

172
00:15:28,490 --> 00:15:33,244
What do you say?
Want to help me make your boy fly?

173
00:15:37,791 --> 00:15:38,625
What?

174
00:15:38,708 --> 00:15:39,918
Incoming call from Lucy.

175
00:15:40,001 --> 00:15:42,837
Now is seriously not the time!

176
00:15:49,010 --> 00:15:51,596
No time. Militech's coming.

177
00:15:51,680 --> 00:15:54,349
How do you know that? Where are you?

178
00:15:54,432 --> 00:15:55,684
They're after me too.

179
00:16:16,913 --> 00:16:17,747
Lucy!

180
00:16:17,831 --> 00:16:18,832
What did she say?

181
00:16:18,915 --> 00:16:22,919
"Use the cyberskeleton
if you want to survive."

182
00:16:23,003 --> 00:16:24,004
The fuck?

183
00:16:24,087 --> 00:16:25,714
She didn't seem herself though.

184
00:16:25,797 --> 00:16:26,756
Sure about that?

185
00:16:26,840 --> 00:16:31,803
Someone's after her too.
I've gotta install it.

186
00:16:31,886 --> 00:16:34,764
Whole truck's a mobile installation unit.

187
00:16:35,473 --> 00:16:38,143
That deck's got the installer all set up.

188
00:16:38,226 --> 00:16:40,437
You are not gonna install this thing!

189
00:16:40,520 --> 00:16:42,105
I gotta get us out of this!

190
00:16:42,188 --> 00:16:46,693
Are you insane?! You don't even know
what this hunk of metal can do!

191
00:16:47,277 --> 00:16:49,779
I don't see any other option.

192
00:16:49,863 --> 00:16:51,948
Besides me knocking you the fuck out?!

193
00:16:52,032 --> 00:16:54,284
I'm gonna go get our car.

194
00:16:54,367 --> 00:16:55,201
I'll go with.

195
00:16:55,285 --> 00:16:56,536
Thanks!

196
00:16:56,619 --> 00:17:01,082
Last time I installed something that
wasn't mine, Maine beat the shit outta me.

197
00:17:02,542 --> 00:17:04,210
Some things just don't change!

198
00:17:04,294 --> 00:17:08,131
Don't! Wait…

199
00:17:10,925 --> 00:17:14,471
You fucking gonk!
Why don't you ever listen?!

200
00:17:21,978 --> 00:17:25,231
What's Militech waiting for?

201
00:17:25,315 --> 00:17:27,734
Kiwi, you able to get eyes on…

202
00:17:29,319 --> 00:17:30,820
Sorry.

203
00:17:44,417 --> 00:17:45,543
What?!

204
00:18:17,784 --> 00:18:20,954
Did you truly think
we would put no failsafe in place?

205
00:18:38,847 --> 00:18:42,600
Shall I open a second neural port
in the back of your skull?

206
00:18:45,061 --> 00:18:48,106
-I'm afraid she's currently indisposed.
-Faraday?!

207
00:18:48,189 --> 00:18:50,608
I trust the job is going well?

208
00:18:50,692 --> 00:18:53,111
Fuck you, put Lucy back on!

209
00:18:53,695 --> 00:18:58,449
This chairjock bitch should feel grateful
to be kissing the ground.

210
00:18:58,533 --> 00:19:02,912
I was worried I might've
overscrambled her brain.

211
00:19:02,996 --> 00:19:05,206
Take your fucking foot off her!

212
00:19:05,290 --> 00:19:08,626
Don't be so serious.
I'm just having a ball of a time.

213
00:19:08,710 --> 00:19:13,131
Besides, I won't have to lift a finger
when Arasaka's done with her.

214
00:19:13,214 --> 00:19:14,883
Faraday!

215
00:19:16,467 --> 00:19:18,386
You're rapidly degenerating!

216
00:19:18,469 --> 00:19:21,222
At this rate, you're gonna
go psycho in seconds!

217
00:19:21,306 --> 00:19:25,852
Elite Militech forces are closing in.

218
00:19:25,935 --> 00:19:30,231
Install the soft, use the cyberskeleton,
David. Lead your crew to safety.

219
00:19:30,315 --> 00:19:36,237
Personally, I think it's beyond you.
Clearly Arasaka sees something I don't.

220
00:19:36,821 --> 00:19:43,036
If you're truly so special, boy,
show me what you can do. Survive.

221
00:19:45,330 --> 00:19:49,375
I'll kill him! I'm gonna go kill him!

222
00:19:50,210 --> 00:19:53,379
I'll kill him! I'll kill him…

223
00:19:53,963 --> 00:19:56,007
I'm gonna fucking--

224
00:19:59,093 --> 00:20:00,470
You okay?

225
00:20:00,553 --> 00:20:02,138
I'm gonna go save Lucy.

226
00:20:02,222 --> 00:20:05,433
Uhh… Nope, I think your brain's fried.

227
00:20:05,516 --> 00:20:09,520
Faraday's double-crossed us.
He's got Lucy.

228
00:20:09,604 --> 00:20:11,439
Huh? What do you mean?

229
00:20:11,522 --> 00:20:14,609
That fucker.
I'm gonna fucking put him in the ground!

230
00:20:14,692 --> 00:20:16,736
I swear, he's gonna fucking die…

231
00:20:16,819 --> 00:20:17,654
David…

232
00:20:19,572 --> 00:20:21,241
Falco! What happened?

233
00:20:21,324 --> 00:20:22,951
Kiwi got me.

234
00:20:23,034 --> 00:20:23,910
What?!

235
00:20:23,993 --> 00:20:26,204
She led us into a trap.

236
00:20:26,287 --> 00:20:29,249
Oh, that hag. She's in it too?

237
00:20:29,332 --> 00:20:31,501
She's a fucking flatline
when I see her next!

238
00:20:37,924 --> 00:20:39,425
Here we go again!

239
00:20:41,719 --> 00:20:42,887
Shit!

240
00:20:42,971 --> 00:20:45,139
Militech's really out to kill us!

241
00:20:45,807 --> 00:20:49,018
I've never seen anything like this.

242
00:20:49,102 --> 00:20:51,312
How can anyone walk with this on?

243
00:20:51,396 --> 00:20:56,150
Two compact thrusters're built in.
Same kind you get on an AV.

244
00:20:56,234 --> 00:21:00,989
On top of that, Arasaka engineered in
a gravity modification prototype.

245
00:21:03,700 --> 00:21:08,371
It can generate unidirectional
grav fields, magnetic forces, too…

246
00:21:09,038 --> 00:21:11,124
That's the magnetic force generator?

247
00:21:16,004 --> 00:21:19,132
Hot damn!
He just mowed a small squad down!

248
00:21:19,215 --> 00:21:22,468
He's using his Sandevistan, too.

249
00:21:44,907 --> 00:21:46,075
He's flying!

250
00:21:46,159 --> 00:21:47,827
That's the gravitational field?

251
00:21:54,334 --> 00:21:56,544
But this tech hasn't left
its testing stage.

252
00:21:57,337 --> 00:21:59,172
The controls are too complex.

253
00:21:59,255 --> 00:22:03,843
There's no guarantee that the equipper's
nerves will be able to withstand it.

254
00:22:03,926 --> 00:22:07,638
It requires an insane level
of mental fortitude against implants.

255
00:22:07,722 --> 00:22:10,641
A one-way ticket to
cyberpsychosis, you mean.

256
00:22:22,362 --> 00:22:23,905
They got him?!

257
00:22:24,530 --> 00:22:25,907
David…

258
00:22:34,373 --> 00:22:35,666
He's still going!

259
00:22:35,750 --> 00:22:38,002
His body is, but…

260
00:22:38,086 --> 00:22:43,341
The more he uses it, the closer he will be
to overloading his cyberware capacity.

261
00:22:43,424 --> 00:22:48,221
But in exchange, the short-term
power it generates is…

262
00:22:52,016 --> 00:22:55,436
unlike anything devised
on this side of sanity.

263
00:23:05,029 --> 00:23:06,280
David?

264
00:23:12,328 --> 00:23:15,498
We're going after Faraday
for betraying us.

265
00:23:15,581 --> 00:23:17,333
And we're gonna save Lucy.

266
00:23:17,959 --> 00:23:19,043
You say that but…

267
00:23:19,127 --> 00:23:21,003
Equal share of the pot.

268
00:23:22,213 --> 00:23:24,465
That's my style.

269
00:23:27,009 --> 00:23:28,886
Alright, buddy.

270
00:23:29,679 --> 00:23:31,722
Onwards to hell.
